    "The distribution of contraceptive methods reveals that no contraceptive method is the most common outcome, accounting for 58.1% of respondents, while 37.9% reported using a modern contraceptive method. Traditional (3.8%) and folkloric (0.2%) methods are used by only a small minority of women.\n",
