    "The severe imbalance among the four classes indicates that a multiclass prediction problem would be challenging, particularly for the folkloric category. Since modern contraceptive use is the primary indicator monitored by national family planning programmes, reframing the modelling task as modern user versus non-modern user provides a more practical and policy-relevant objective.\n"
